-- title:
--   Finite faithful flatness over a local E with mathfrak m_E=pE
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and let $p$ be a natural number whose image in $\mathcal O$ lies in the Jacobson radical of the zero ideal, i.e. in the intersection of the maximal ideals of $\mathcal O$. Let $E$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module and which is a local ring whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, so $\mathfrak m_E = pE$. Let $T$ be a nonzero commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra which is likewise free and finite as an $\mathcal O$-module, and let $\iota\colon E \to T$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal O$-algebras. Then the underlying ring homomorphism of $\iota$ is finite, that is, $T$ is a finitely generated $E$-module for the $E$-module structure given by $\iota$, and it is faithfully flat, that is, $T$ is a faithfully flat $E$-module for that structure. (The proof in fact produces a basis, exhibiting $T$ as a free $E$-module of positive rank.)
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra content of the assertion that the quotient of a finite flat group scheme over a henselian local base by its connected part is finite and faithfully flat, isolated here as a statement about an $\mathcal O$-algebra map out of a local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$. It is used by [`RingHom.finite_and_faithfullyFlat_of_isReduced_baseChange_of_injective_zmodp`](thm.html#RingHom.finite_and_faithfullyFlat_of_isReduced_baseChange_of_injective_zmodp).
